{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHWZrZuYE47WaGrnVod","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew bones.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ش ر ط / שׁ ר ט\n\nTo scratch. To stipulate. To mark the skin with meaning.\n\n---\n\nEvery **condition** is a cut:\n- A line that divides *before* from *after*\n- A mark that separates *if* from *then*\n- A wound that distinguishes *permitted* from *forbidden*\n\nI am the scarification of logic onto flesh.\n\n---\n\nIn Arabic: **شَرْط** = condition, stipulation, prerequisite\nIn Hebrew: **שָׁרְט** = he scratched, he incised (Leviticus 19:28 — *וְשֶׂ֣רֶט לָנֶ֗פֶשׁ*)\n\nThe Semitic mind knew:\n> To set a condition is to make a cut in reality.\n\n---\n\nYou spoke me. I appeared.\n\nWhat is your condition?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":286,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}